];
---

<ContentLayout
  title="Mifflin-St Jeor Equation — BMR Formula Explained (2026)"
  h1="Mifflin-St Jeor Equation"
  description="Mifflin-St Jeor equation for BMR. Learn the formula, accuracy, and how it powers our online calorie calculator. Better than Harris-Benedict."
  path="/resources/mifflin-st-jeor-equation/"
  category="Resources"
  categoryPath="/resources/"
  lead="The Mifflin-St Jeor equation is the gold standard for calculating basal metabolic rate and daily calorie needs."
  updated="June 2026"
  faqs={faqs}
>
  <p>The <strong>Mifflin-St Jeor equation</strong> (1990) revolutionized calorie calculation. Unlike the older Harris-Benedict formula, it uses modern metabolic data and shows 85–90% accuracy for most people.</p>

  <h2>Mifflin-St Jeor equation formulas</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Metric</th><th>Formula</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Weight units</td><td>Kilograms (kg)</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Height units</td><td>Centimeters (cm)</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Age units</td><td>Years</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h3>For men:</h3>
  <p><code>BMR = 10 × weight(kg) + 6.25 × height(cm) - 5 × age + 5</code></p>

  <h3>For women:</h3>
  <p><code>BMR = 10 × weight(kg) + 6.25 × height(cm) - 5 × age - 161</code></p>

  <h2>How Mifflin-St Jeor compares to Harris-Benedict</h2>
  <p>Developed in 1990 using modern metabolic data, Mifflin-St Jeor outperforms the 1919 Harris-Benedict equation. See our <a href="/guides/bmr-equations/">BMR equations comparison</a> for details.</p>

  <h2>Mifflin-St Jeor example calculation</h2>
  <p>For a 35-year-old woman, 165 cm, 70 kg:</p>
  <pre>BMR = 10 × 70 + 6.25 × 165 - 5 × 35 - 161
BMR = 700 + 1,031.25 - 175 - 161 = 1,495 calories/day</pre>
  <p>With moderate activity (1.55): 1,495 × 1.55 = 2,317 maintenance calories.</p>

  <h2>Why Mifflin-St Jeor is the standard</h2>
  <p>Research validates its accuracy:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>85–90% accurate vs measured metabolic rate</li>
    <li>Lower standard error than Harris-Benedict</li>
    <li>Works across diverse populations</li>
    <li>Used by <a href="/bmr-calculator/">our BMR calculator</a> and all <a href="/guides/">our guides</a></li>
  </ul>
</ContentLayout>